    "created_at": "2026-01-12T10:40:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-12T10:43:57Z",
    "body": "What #11952 did was to make sure that there _always_ is a method tracker, regardless of how a navigation was started (I really should've changed the name to navigation tracker, since it becomes a tracker of all navigations not just those initiated from one of the Navigation API navigation methods). It has nothing to do with interception, and since there _always_ is a tracker it's always possible to clean it up, making that otherwise superfluous. That's why `#commit-an-intercepted-navigate-event` starts out asserting that apiMethodTracker is not null.\n\nSo only reverting #11987 should be enough, which in turn makes #12022 a won't fix.\n\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
